{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.62,
   "text": "I drive a school bus on a dark country route, long before the sun comes up."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.22,
   "end": 14.105,
   "text": "The driver who had it before me left one rule, scratched into the sun visor."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.705,
   "end": 19.676,
   "text": "If anything knocks on the back emergency door... don't stop. And don't look."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.576,
   "end": 25.867,
   "text": "All fall, it was easy. Sleepy kids. Frosty fields. Twelve quiet stops."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.467,
   "end": 31.544,
   "text": "Then one morning in December, out between the last farm and the river bridge..."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 34.344,
   "end": 37.693,
   "text": "three slow knocks... from the back of the bus."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.693,
   "end": 42.192,
   "text": "Every kid went silent. Every single one."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.192,
   "end": 46.691,
   "text": "I gripped the wheel, and kept my eyes on the road."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.491,
   "end": 53.032,
   "text": "Three more knocks. Slower this time... patient."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.232,
   "end": 58.605,
   "text": "Then nothing. Just the engine, and my own breathing, for miles."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 60.205,
   "end": 65.496,
   "text": "At the school, the kids filed off like always, and I finally let go of the wheel."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.096,
   "end": 71.451,
   "text": "Until the last little girl stopped on the steps... and looked back down the empty aisle."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.451,
   "end": 75.587,
   "text": "'Mister,' she whispered. 'Why didn't you let him out?'"
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 77.387,
   "end": 81.781,
   "text": "Behind me, very softly... three knocks. From the very back seat."
  }
 ],
